# pilot_labels — hand-written tactical captions for 30 stratified ticks.
# Format: one JSON per line.
# Required fields: demo_stem, round_num, tick (downsampled 8 Hz tick index), caption.
# Optional field: match_id (HLTV numeric match ID; helps disambiguate but not required).
#
# Suggested stratification (5 per category):
#   - eco / save round
#   - mid-round (default / lurk / probe)
#   - execute / commitment moment
#   - post-plant defense / retake setup
#   - retake attempt
#   - clutch (1vN)
#
# Replace the examples below with real labels from data you have access to.
# Demo stems should match exactly what appears in HF tick_sequences metas.
# To verify a label is loadable, run: python scripts/pilot_minimum.py --labels <this>
#
# Example rows (REPLACE — these are placeholders, not real labels):
